---
description: Modern React 19 component rules. Function components, hooks discipline, no unnecessary effects.
globs: **/*.tsx, **/*.jsx
alwaysApply: false
---

# React components

- Function components and hooks only. No class components.
- One component per file for anything non-trivial; name the file after the component.
- Derive values during render instead of syncing them with `useEffect` + `useState`. Effects are for synchronising with external systems only.
- Don't fetch in `useEffect` if the project has a data layer (TanStack Query, SWR, RSC, loaders). Use it.
- Keys must be stable IDs, never array indexes for lists that can reorder.
- Lift state only as far as needed. Prefer composition (children/props) over context; use context for genuinely global values.
- Don't add `useMemo` / `useCallback` by default; add them when there's a measured problem or a referential-equality requirement. (React Compiler handles most cases.)
- Forms: use `<form action>` / `useActionState` (React 19) or the project's form library. Every input has a label.
- Accessibility: semantic elements (`button`, not clickable `div`), alt text, focus states, keyboard support.
- Type props with a `type Props = {...}`; no `React.FC`.
